# fm84 v slovenščini.
#
# Each msgid is the English as the code has it, and the msgstr under it what
# is shown in its place. A sentence with a count in it has a msgstr for each
# form the count takes, by its last two digits: [one] for 1, 101; [two] for
# 2, 102; [few] for 3, 4, 103, 104; [other] for the rest. A msgctxt sets one
# use of a word apart from the same word elsewhere. {name} is a place the
# program fills, kept as it is. The letters to press - Y, N, A and the like
# - stay as they are, and so do the names of the keys. Names are quoted
# »thus«.

